{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0014855","label":"intellectual disability, autosomal dominant 42","definition":"Any autosomal dominant intellectual disability in which the cause of the disease is a heterozygous mutation in the GNB1 gene. It is characterized by global developmental delay, intellectual disability, hypotonia, structural brain abnormalities, and seizures. Other less common findings include dystonia, visual impairment, behavior problems, growth delay, craniofacial defects, and genitourinary abnormalities in males.","synonyms":["GNB1 autosomal dominant non-syndromic intellectual disability","GNB1-related disorder","GNB1-related neurodevelopmental disorder","MRD42","autosomal dominant intellectual disability 42","autosomal dominant non-syndromic intellectual disability 42","autosomal dominant non-syndromic intellectual disability caused by mutation in GNB1","global developmental delay-neuro-ophthalmological abnormalities-seizures-intellectual disability syndrome"],"xrefs":["DOID:0070072","GARD:0018501","MEDGEN:934741","OMIM:616973","Orphanet:488613","UMLS:C4310774"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":83,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_9a6324a91775","source":"MONDO:0014855","target":"GNB1","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:488613","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/488613","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed) — G protein subunit beta 1"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:616973","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://omim.org/entry/616973","snippet":"GNB1 is annotated as disease gene of OMIM:616973 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, OMIM-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["OMIM","Orphanet"],"level":"curated"}],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":"e_6e